      "extract": "Preliminaries We fix a positive integer n. A partition is a sequence λ = (a1, . . . , am) of non-negative integers such that a1 ≥a2 ≥· · · ≥am. We identify partitions that only differ by a string of zeros at the end. We say that λ is a partition of n if |λ| := a1+a2+· · ·+am = n. We denote by Pn the set of partitions of n and by P := S∞ i=0 Pi the set of all partitions. If µ = (c1, . . . , cl) is another partition",
